WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.428
Straighten the contour contributions.

00:00:02.428 --> 00:00:05.179
Follow four successive arcs of the inner ellipse.

00:00:05.179 --> 00:00:10.085
For each arc, integrate the complex density, including the oriented tangent.

00:00:10.085 --> 00:00:13.946
In the output plane each coloured arrow is one such increment.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.353
Join them head to tail.

00:00:15.353 --> 00:00:18.809
The displacement from start to finish gives the coefficient.

00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:22.605
Now turn the arrows until they all face right, keeping their lengths.

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:27.170
The straightened path can be longer because the original arrows partly cancel.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:32.439
Splitting into finer arcs gives the integral of the absolute density as an upper bound.

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:34.928
Replace the local heights by ceilings.

00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:39.408
At each boundary point the absolute density contains three factors.

00:00:39.408 --> 00:00:42.074
The first is the modulus of the function.

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:45.934
Its height on the inner rim stays below the outer supremum, M rho.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.537
The second is the modulus of the kernel.

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:52.291
Bound every height by the largest kernel height on this inner rim.

00:00:52.291 --> 00:00:54.765
The third is the speed of the moving point.

00:00:54.765 --> 00:00:58.113
Integrating that speed over one turn gives the perimeter.

00:00:58.113 --> 00:01:01.036
Those three pieces give the estimate on the screen.

00:01:01.336 --> 00:01:03.418
Every second frequency survives.

00:01:03.418 --> 00:01:05.636
Look inside the kernel at degree three.

00:01:05.636 --> 00:01:08.558
The first three frequencies are four, six and eight.

00:01:08.558 --> 00:01:13.059
At one moving point each coloured ridge gives the real part of its wave.

00:01:13.059 --> 00:01:16.003
The matching arrow carries the whole complex value.

00:01:16.003 --> 00:01:18.818
Its length is sigma times s to the minus k.

00:01:18.818 --> 00:01:22.935
A full turn rotates the fourth frequency four times clockwise.

00:01:22.935 --> 00:01:25.771
All three arrows have fixed lengths at this radius.

00:01:25.771 --> 00:01:28.565
Their sum changes as their directions change.

00:01:28.565 --> 00:01:32.661
To bound it at every angle, add their lengths and include the rest of the ladder.

00:01:32.961 --> 00:01:34.958
Sum the geometric majorant.

00:01:34.958 --> 00:01:38.584
For general degree n, the first frequency is n plus one.

00:01:38.584 --> 00:01:42.232
Replace each nonnegative sigma by its upper bound of two.

00:01:42.232 --> 00:01:47.906
Successive upper bounds have ratio one over s squared, since the exponents differ by two.

00:01:47.906 --> 00:01:54.369
The first upper bound divided by one minus that ratio sums the entire geometric series.

00:01:54.369 --> 00:02:01.067
Simplify the fraction to get two times s to the minus n divided by s minus its reciprocal.

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:04.224
Insert this kernel ceiling into the contour estimate.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:07.509
The two cancels the two in the contour normalization.

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:12.714
What remains is the perimeter constant, the function norm, and the geometric decay.

